.TH htsserver 1 "07 October 2026" "httrack website copier"
.SH NAME
htsserver \- web server for the WebHTTrack interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B htsserver <path\-to\-html\-root\-dir> [option value ..] [key value ..]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B htsserver
serves the WebHTTrack interface, a set of HTML pages that drive the
.BR httrack (1)
engine from a web browser. It listens on 127.0.0.1 by default and prints the address to open on a line starting with
.IR URL= .
Most users start it through
.BR webhttrack (1),
which also opens the browser.
.PP
The first argument is the directory that holds the interface pages and the language files, usually
.IR /usr/share/httrack/ .
The options and the key/value pairs come after it. The help and version options must come first instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-port <port>
listen on this port (default: the first free port from 8080)
.TP
.B \-\-bind <address>
listen on this address (default: 127.0.0.1)
.TP
.B \-\-ppid <pid>
exit once the interface is closed; pid is the launcher's
.TP
.B \-\-ping\-timeout <secs>
with \-\-ppid, how long a silent browser window counts as open (default: 120)
.TP
.B key value
any other pair sets a value the interface reads, such as path or lang
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
print this help and exit
.TP
.B \-\-version
print the version and exit
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B htsserver /usr/share/httrack/ path \(dq$HOME/websites\(dq lang 1
serve the interface in English, and keep projects in ~/websites
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Each mirror started from the interface writes its errors and warnings to
.I hts\-log.txt
in the project directory.
.SH BUGS
Please reports bugs to
.B <bugs@httrack.com>.
Include a complete, self-contained example that will allow the bug to be reproduced, and say which version of httrack you are using. Do not forget to detail options used, OS version, and any other information you deem necessary.
